<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Audit assistant — Icones</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../static/style.css">
<style>
  .assist-wrap { max-width: var(--maxw-prose); margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.25rem var(--gutter) 4rem; }
  .assist-back { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-mute); text-decoration: none; }
  .assist-back:hover { color: var(--link-hover); }
  .assist-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-elev); box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; margin: 1.1rem 0;
  }
  .assist-card h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .assist-cta {
    display: inline-block; margin: 0.35rem 0 0.2rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .assist-cta:hover { color: #fff; filter: brightness(1.12); }
  .assist-meta { color: var(--fg-faint); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .assist-steps li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body class="theme-auto">
<div class="assist-wrap">
  <p><a class="assist-back" href="../index.html">← Icones auditor dashboard</a></p>
  <h1>Audit assistant</h1>
  <p>
    Two ways to ask an LLM questions about this formalization while you audit —
    both grounded in <em>this site's own build data</em> ({{N_ENTRIES}} entries,
    {{N_DEPENDS}} statement-level dependency edges, commit <code>{{COMMIT}}</code>),
    and both running on <strong>your own Claude account</strong>: a free or Pro
    claude.ai login is enough, no API key involved.
  </p>

  <div class="assist-card">
    <h2>1 · Chat now</h2>
    <p>
      The chat page is hosted on claude.ai. Open it, sign in with your Claude
      account, and ask away — the assistant looks entries, statuses, and
      dependencies up in the dashboard's data before answering, and links every
      claim back to an entry page here.
    </p>
    <p><a class="assist-cta" href="{{ARTIFACT_URL}}">Open the chat assistant ↗</a></p>
    <p class="assist-meta">
      Your first question triggers a one-time permission prompt from claude.ai;
      usage counts against your own plan. The conversation lives in your browser
      tab only.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="assist-card">
    <h2>2 · Prewarm your own Claude with the audit skill</h2>
    <p>
      Prefer chatting in claude.ai directly (or in Claude Code)? Download the
      generated skill — it packages the entry index, the dependency relation, and
      the verification guide as a Claude skill.
    </p>
    <p><a class="assist-cta" href="{{SKILL_ZIP_URL}}">Download icones-audit-skill.zip</a></p>
    <ol class="assist-steps">
      <li>On claude.ai: <em>Settings → Capabilities → Skills → Upload skill</em>, pick the zip.</li>
      <li>Ask about Icones in any chat — Claude loads the skill when relevant.</li>
      <li>In Claude Code: unzip into your project's <code>.claude/skills/</code> instead.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="assist-card">
    <h2>Why you can trust it to be in sync</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is written by hand twice. The skill, the chat page's data pack,
      and this site are all generated by the same build from the same sources
      (<code>docs/*.md</code> and the Rocq <code>.glob</code> files): every deploy
      regenerates all of them together. The dependency answers use the same
      statement-level relation the <a href="../graph.html">graph</a> draws —
      references made only inside proof scripts are excluded by design.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="assist-meta">Generated at commit <code>{{COMMIT}}</code>, {{BUILT_AT}} · {{TAB_COUNTS}}</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
